ssues), applies defaults,\nand the admin UI \u002F MCP render forms from the schema (trigger.dev model).\n",[169,249,250],{},"input_schema"," is persisted on the task row (sqlite v0.9, mysql\u002Fpg v7; mongo\nis schemaless).",[174,253,255],{"id":254},"_2026-08-26-cancel-on-poll-timeout-wave-core-0530-daemon-0121","2026-08-26 — cancel-on-poll-timeout wave (core 0.53.0 \u002F daemon 0.12.1)",[179,257,258],{},[182,259,260,263,264,267,268,271,272,275,276,279,280,283,284,286],{},[158,261,262],{},"Cancel-on-timeout"," — a poll\u002Frun timeout is no longer a silent stop-polling:\nwhen the accepted envelope advertised a ",[169,265,266],{},"cancelUrl",", sched POSTs ",[169,269,270],{},"{ runId }","\nto the worker ",[158,273,274],{},"before"," failing the timed-out run, so the worker halts at the\nnext stage boundary instead of finishing destructive work after the ",[169,277,278],{},"failed","\nverdict was recorded. A failed cancel signal is appended to the run error\n(",[169,281,282],{},"cancel signal failed: \u003Creason>","). Workers without a ",[169,285,266],{}," keep the\nlegacy stop-polling semantics.",[174,288,290],{"id":289},"_2026-08-25-sync-health-release-hardening-core-0520-daemon-0120-storage-mongo-051","2026-08-25 — sync health + release hardening (core 0.52.0 \u002F daemon 0.12.0 \u002F storage-mongo 0.5.1)",[179,292,293,311,325],{},[182,294,295,302,303,306,307,310],{},[158,296,297,298,301],{},"Sync-health alerts (",[169,299,300],{},"sync.failed",")"," — the daemon reports tasks.json sync\nfailures over the alerts webhook (",[169,304,305],{},"onSyncFailed",", default on): a dead storage\npool means nothing schedules, so ",[169,308,309],{},"run.failed"," alerts can never fire — sync\nhealth is the scheduler's own heartbeat. Fires once per failure streak\n(dedupe), resets on heal. Prod lesson 2026-08-24.",[182,312,313,316,317,320,321,324],{},[158,314,315],{},"Mongo reconnect ownership"," — the adapter, not the driver's SDAM, owns\nreconnection: connection-class errors force a fresh topology\n(",[169,318,319],{},"client.close()"," + ",[169,322,323],{},"client.connect()",") and retry (bounded, 2×).",[182,326,327,330,331,334,335,338,339,342],{},[158,328,329],{},"Release hardening"," — ",[169,332,333],{},"--retention-ttl 0"," truly means \"retention off\"\n(previously ",[169,336,337],{},"0"," was falsy-dropped and the default TTL applied); ",[169,340,341],{},"yarn publish:check"," verifies artifacts reached the registry after publish; public\ndocs cleanup (README quick start, LICENSE MIT, CONTRIBUTING).",[174,344,346],{"id":345},"_2026-08-23-prod-cutover-fixes-daemon-0110-core-050x-storage-mongo-050","2026-08-23 — prod-cutover fixes (daemon 0.11.0 \u002F core 0.50.x \u002F storage-mongo 0.5.0)",[154,348,349],{},"First wave driven by production findings from a real deployment:",[179,351,352,362,375,383,389],{},[182,353,354,357,358,361],{},[158,355,356],{},"Crash resilience"," — engine error boundary around dispatches; admin API\ncatches handler errors; Mongo storage reconnects (",[169,359,360],{},"MONGO_RETRY_MS",").",[182,363,364,367,368,243,371,374],{},[158,365,366],{},"Sort indexes"," on ",[169,369,370],{},"name",[169,372,373],{},"startedAt"," for run listing.",[182,376,377,382],{},[158,378,379],{},[169,380,381],{},"timeoutMs: -1"," = no timeout (per-task run deadline contract).",[182,384,385,388],{},[158,386,387],{},"Log coercion"," — run logs normalized to strings.",[182,390,391,395],{},[158,392,393],{},[169,394,333],{}," = retention off.",[174,397,399],{"id":398},"_2026-08-22-dispatch-view-daemon-image-from-npm-daemon-010x-core-0490-storage-040","2026-08-22 — dispatch view + daemon image from npm (daemon 0.10.x \u002F core 0.49.0 \u002F storage-* 0.4.0)",[179,401,402,414,431],{},[182,403,404,330,407,243,410,413],{},[158,405,406],{},"Dispatch view",[169,408,409],{},"triggerTask",[169,411,412],{},"retryRun"," apply per-run data\u002Fbody\noverrides the same way scheduled dispatches do.",[182,415,416,422,423,426,427,430],{},[158,417,418,421],{},[169,419,420],{},"--storage"," bridge"," — the daemon selects its storage adapter from the CLI\n(",[169,424,425],{},"--storage mongo|mysql|postgres|\u003Ccustom module>","); credentials come from env,\nnever from process arguments. BYO adapters via ",[169,428,429],{},"createStorage(env)"," helpers.",[182,432,433,330,436,439,440,443],{},[158,434,435],{},"Official Docker image built from npm",[169,437,438],{},"FROM @sched\u002Fdaemon"," composition,\n",[169,441,442],{},"docker-cli"," included (Docker runner works inside the container).",[174,445,447],{"id":446},"_2026-08-21-cancellation-that-reaches-the-worker-core-047048-daemon-0709","2026-08-21 — cancellation that reaches the worker (core 0.47–0.48 \u002F daemon 0.7–0.9)",[179,449,450,472,494],{},[182,451,452,457,458,461,462,465,466,468,469,471],{},[158,453,454,456],{},[169,455,266],{}," channel"," — async workers can opt into receiving a cancel\nsignal: sched ",[169,459,460],{},"POST","s ",[169,463,464],{},"{runId}"," to ",[169,467,266],{}," before finishing the run as\ncancelled. Without ",[169,470,266],{},": legacy stop-polling (documented).",[182,473,474,330,477,480,481,243,484,487,488,243,491,361],{},[158,475,476],{},"Cancel observability",[169,478,479],{},"[cancel]"," log lines (",[169,482,483],{},"cancel-sent",[169,485,486],{},"cancel-ack","\n\u002F ",[169,489,490],{},"cancel-failed",[169,492,493],{},"cancel-no-channel",[182,495,496,499],{},[158,497,498],{},"Dispatcher fix"," — the daemon forwards cancel to the per-task runner\n(previously the signal never left the daemon when the runner was wrapped).",[174,501,503],{"id":502},"_2026-08-20-run-deadlines-http-runner-hardening-core-045046-daemon-060","2026-08-20 — run deadlines + HTTP runner hardening (core 0.45–0.46 \u002F daemon 0.6.0)",[179,505,506,531],{},[182,507,508,511,512,515,516,519,520,523,524,527,528,361],{},[158,509,510],{},"Per-task run deadline"," (",[169,513,514],{},"timeoutMs","): ",[169,517,518],{},"-1"," = never auto-terminate (default\nwhen absent), ",[169,521,522],{},">0"," = forced failure after N ms, ",[169,525,526],{},"absent"," = legacy. Storage\nschema migration to v6 (",[169,529,530],{},"timeout_ms",[182,532,533,535,536,538,539,542,543,546],{},[158,534,41],{},": envelope responses from broken workers → run ",[169,537,278],{}," (not\nsilent success); relative ",[169,540,541],{},"statusUrl"," resolves against ",[169,544,545],{},"config.url","; transient\npoll errors (network \u002F 5xx \u002F 408 \u002F 429) retried (2 × 500 ms).",[174,548,550],{"id":549},"_2026-08-18-control-plane-cli-admin-api-010-cli-010-daemon-03x","2026-08-18 — control plane + CLI (admin-api 0.1.0 \u002F cli 0.1.0 \u002F daemon 0.3.x)",[179,552,553,560,574],{},[182,554,555,556,559],{},"Admin REST control plane extracted into ",[169,557,558],{},"@sched\u002Fadmin-api"," (OpenAPI spec,\ntyped client).",[182,561,562,563,511,566,569,570,573],{},"Operator CLI ",[169,564,565],{},"@sched\u002Fcli",[169,567,568],{},"sched status","), ",[169,571,572],{},"schedd"," entry junction-safe.",[182,575,576,577,580,581,584,585,361],{},"Node engine floor raised to ",[169,578,579],{},">= 24"," in the daemon wave (",[169,582,583],{},">= 22.5"," in core for\n",[169,586,587],{},"node:sqlite",[174,589,591],{"id":590},"earlier-foundations","Earlier — foundations",[179,593,594,607,613,620,632,645,660,670],{},[182,595,596,511,599,602,603,606],{},[158,597,598],{},"Engine",[169,600,601],{},"@sched\u002Fcore","): queue-based execution, retries with backoff,\npriority, run history, ",[169,604,605],{},"onRunFinal"," alerts, lock\u002Fheartbeat, live-sync\nrecovery, internal\u002Fprocess runners.",[182,608,609,612],{},[158,610,611],{},"Storages",": SQLite (default), MariaDB\u002FMySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB — split\ninto per-adapter packages with a shared contract suite.",[182,614,615,511,617,619],{},[158,616,117],{},[169,618,558],{},"): tasks\u002Fruns\u002Fschedules REST, Bearer auth,\ntriggered-by forwarding.",[182,621,622,511,624,627,628,631],{},[158,623,129],{},[169,625,626],{},"@sched\u002Fmcp","): 9 tools over the admin API, stdio + Streamable\nHTTP, ",[169,629,630],{},"--readonly"," guard.",[182,633,634,511,637,640,641,644],{},[158,635,636],{},"Web UI",[169,638,639],{},"@sched\u002Fui","): standalone ",[169,642,643],{},"sched-ui serve",", embeddable web\ncomponents.",[182,646,647,649,650,652,653,656,657,361],{},[158,648,31],{},": request\u002Fresponse envelope, async runs via ",[169,651,541],{},"\npolling, idempotency via ",[169,654,655],{},"x-sched-run-id",", outbound auth (",[169,658,659],{},"x-sched-api-key",[182,661,662,665,666,669],{},[158,663,664],{},"Docker \u002F SSH \u002F process runners","; ",[169,667,668],{},"config.network"," for Docker runner.",[182,671,672,675,676,679],{},[158,673,674],{},"Docs",": Docus 5 site, ",[169,677,678],{},"llms.txt"," for AI agents, self-hosting + security guides.",{"title":681,"searchDepth":21,"depth":21,"links":682},"",[683,684,685,686,687,688,689,690,691],{"id":176,"depth":21,"text":177},{"id":254,"depth":21,"text":255},{"id":289,"depth":21,"text":290},{"id":345,"depth":21,"text":346},{"id":398,"depth":21,"text":399},{"id":446,"depth":21,"text":447},{"id":502,"depth":21,"text":503},{"id":549,"depth":21,"text":550},{"id":590,"depth":21,"text":591},"Version history — release notes for every sched wave, newest first","md",null,{},{"order":8},{"title":5,"description":692},"rfDd6lr7Ptb8xfpaOWGDkAlFsw5bjqcYgDvavS21lQU",[694,700],{"title":10,"path":11,"stem":12,"description":701,"children":-1},"What sched is and how it works",1789814222078]